<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chahamanas of Shakambhari</h1><p class="st-meta">650 CE – 1194 CE (approx.) · capital Ajmer</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Chauhan Rajput dynasty of Sambhar and Ajmer, whose king Prithviraj Chauhan fought Muhammad of Ghor at Tarain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition names Vasudeva, said to have discovered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambhar-salt-lake">Sambhar</a> salt lake, as the dynasty's founder in the 7th century. The early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> ruled the Sapadalaksha country around Shakambhari, modern Sambhar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, as feudatories of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vigraharaja-ii">Vigraharaja II</a> asserted independence in the 10th century, as recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> inscription of 973.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajayaraja-ii">Ajayaraja</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> around 1113 and made it the capital, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnoraja">Arnoraja</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ana-sagar-lake">Ana Sagar</a> lake. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vigraharaja-iv">Vigraharaja IV</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> from the Tomara dynasty and wrote a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> play inscribed on stone in Ajmer. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/paramara-dynasty">Paramara dynasty</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chaulukya-dynasty">Chaulukya dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavids</a>. Their state rested on a warrior nobility, revenue from agriculture and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambhar-salt-lake">Sambhar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-trade">salt trade</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraja III</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-tarain">first battle of Tarain</a> in 1191, but lost the second in 1192 and was executed. A relative ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> under Ghurid protection until 1194, and the branch at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranthambore-fort">Ranthambore</a> continued. Prithviraj became a hero of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> legend through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-raso">Prithviraj Raso</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chahamanas-of-shakambhari.jpg" alt="Chahamanas of Shakambhari" width="320" height="156"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vigraha_Raja_IV_of_the_Chauhans_of_Ajmer_Circa_1150-1164.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>650 CE – 1194 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ajmer</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ajayaraja, Vigraharaja IV, Prithviraja III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Apabhramsha</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chauhans of Ajmer, Chahamana dynasty, Sapadalaksha</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=922&amp;focus=chahamanas-of-shakambhari" aria-label="Chahamanas of Shakambhari on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6649 1206 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chahamanas of Shakambhari lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path c